## STEP 6 GRADED HONESTLY -- the protection is present; the literal word EXEMPT is NOT on the runner

Invocation: powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .tools/kill-maint.ps1   (DRY RUN,
-Execute NEVER passed), run 2026-10-13T05:55:36Z, exit 0, 68 lines.

WHAT THE OUTPUT SAYS (line 38-41):
  --- deliberate detached jobs: 3 marker(s), 6 worker worktree(s); 0 candidate(s) EXEMPT ---
    MARKER LIVE SCHEDULED Task Scheduler job pid 27560 started 05:52Z

So the EXEMPT COUNT IS ZERO and no "EXEMPT PID 27560" line exists. The order's step 6 says the dry
run "must list the new runner's python process as EXEMPT", and read as those words, IT DOES NOT.

WHY, and it is not a regression: kill-maint's EXEMPT list holds processes that WOULD have been
ORPHAN/NATIVE candidates and were spared (by a worker worktree or a declared detached job). PID
27560 never becomes a candidate at all -- it is recognised earlier as a LIVE SCHEDULED Task
Scheduler job. Exclusion before candidacy is STRONGER than exemption after it, but it prints
differently, and "0 candidate(s) EXEMPT" is the output of a run with nothing to spare.

Round 79's bw1_gc_dryrun.out (lines 285-289) DID print "2 candidate(s) EXEMPT" with
"EXEMPT PID 29192 python.exe WORKTREE .../wk-harvest-runner-pin-b5a7a3a4b6 (command line)". That is
the reading step 6's wording was written against. The criterion's text has outlived the tool's
output shape; this seat is not going to hunt an invocation that manufactures the token.

THE TWO PROTECTIONS THE CRITERION EXISTS TO VERIFY, BOTH MEASURED PRESENT:
  1. THE WORKTREE (the Z-S111 hazard -- the GC removing the pin DIRECTORY under a live runner):
     wk-harvest-runner-pin-1c69fa35a3 reads a `locked` line in git worktree list --porcelain, as do
     b5a7a3a4b6 and c1be67f53c. See bz1_lock.out. A locked worktree is never removed.
  2. THE PROCESS (kill-maint reaping the runner): PID 27560 is listed as MARKER LIVE SCHEDULED and
     the candidate set is EMPTY, so it is not in the kill set.

VERDICT: the GC will not reap this runner or its pin, and that is measured on both planes. Step 6 as
WORDED does not pass, and saying so is the point rather than reading the criterion down to fit.
Filed as row AMGT_HARVST-Z-S116 for the issuer.

